    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Phishing for Information — Login Form Discovery", "technique": "T1598.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-12 09:14:03 CEST, data.srcip=203.0.113.66 began sequentially requesting common authentication-portal paths (/login, /signin, /auth, /sso, /portal, /webmail, /owa, /citrix, /vpn) against the internal web portal 10.108.57.177. Suricata fired 'ET WEB_SERVER Login Page Enumeration' and Wazuh web rules flagged a single external source walking a known login-path wordlist with a fixed desktop Chrome user-agent. Each request was spaced ~12 seconds apart — slow enough to slip under naive rate thresholds, methodical enough to map every authentication surface on the portal. This is the classic phishing-for-information prep step: locate the real login form so it can be cloned into a credential-capture page.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh web rule + Suricata 'Login Page Enumeration' triggered with data.srcip=203.0.113.66 against data.dstip=10.108.57.177 across >6 distinct data.url login-path values within a 5-minute window from a single external source.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:14:03+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Phishing for Information — CSRF Token & Page Structure Harvest", "technique": "T1598.003", "what_happened": "At 09:22:40 CEST, the same data.srcip=203.0.113.66 re-fetched /login and /portal/login specifically, this time parsing the returned HTML for csrf / token / antiforgery markers. Suricata logged repeated GET requests with the same Chrome user-agent harvesting the page structure. Harvesting the CSRF token layout and HTML skeleton is the second phishing-prep step: it lets the attacker build a pixel-accurate clone of the portal login page that even reproduces the anti-forgery field, maximising victim trust.", "chain_reason": "Same data.srcip=203.0.113.66 issuing GET data.url=/login and /portal/login with data.http.method=GET, ~18s apart, immediately following the Step 1 enumeration burst — page-structure reconnaissance pattern.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:22:40+0200"},
